{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210691,"nonce":"LMr18zuTLonAOUeHnJ+0HUI505A=","title":"compile_osr_entries panics \"undefined value vN\": two reachability implementations disagree","message":"During tiered compile of the template package's Parse_.parseStmt_, the beadie broker thread panics at src/codegen/cranelift_backend.rs:1150 with `undefined value v53`, in roughly 18% of runs, while lowering an OSR entry for bb13.\n\nosr_entry_layout decides an OSR entry is emittable by walking blocks reachable from the target and checking every operand is defined in a reachable block, rematerialisable, or in external_args. lower_mir_impl then populates val_map from external_args, rematerialised constants and block params in RPO from the target. The two sides use different reachability code: cranelift_backend.rs `reachable_from` (no bounds guard) vs mir/mod.rs `osr_reachable_blocks` (guards idx \u003c blocks.len()). For parseStmt_'s shape (36 blocks, back-edges at bb13 and bb26, multi-pred target) they diverge: layout thinks v53 (bb13's third block param) is covered, lowering looks it up before the param is appended.\n\nNon-deterministic because the broker races the main thread's pending_callee_precompile queue (engine.rs record_pending_callees), so which functions are in flight together varies.\n\nFix direction: one shared reachability function used by both osr_entry_layout and osr_external_live_values, plus a debug assertion that the layout's covered set equals what lowering actually defines.","files":null}]}